.TH BERYLLIUM-FDE 8 "2026-11-16" "beryllium-tools" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
beryllium-fde \- full disk encryption for Beryllium OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B beryllium-fde prepare
.RB [ \-\-i\-have\-a\-backup ]
.br
.B beryllium-fde live
.br
.B beryllium-fde
.RI [ mode ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Automates the endorsed Beryllium OS full disk encryption layout: an ESP
holding only the GRUB EFI binary, with everything else (grub.cfg, kernel,
initramfs, root btrfs, swap) inside a LUKS2 container. Two keyslots are
used: slot 0 holds the user passphrase with PBKDF2 so GRUB can unlock it,
slot 1 holds a 64-byte keyfile (argon2id) that is embedded into the
encrypted initramfs so the system decrypts itself silently. The only
passphrase prompt is the one at GRUB.
.PP
At every prompt, Ctrl+C and Ctrl+D both count as an abort: the tool
exits without answering the prompt (resumable where progress already
allows it). Running the tool without an argument prints the help menu.
.PP
The conversion is done in place from a live ISO with
.B cryptsetup reencrypt \-\-encrypt \-\-pbkdf pbkdf2
and is resumable: an interrupted run detects the state and continues.
A full disk backup is mandatory before running this tool.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B prepare
Run on the installed (unencrypted) system. Verifies the layout is the
endorsed one (UEFI, GRUB, plain btrfs root, vfat ESP, shrink headroom,
required packages), asks for a backup acknowledgement, and writes the
handoff file
.IR /var/lib/beryllium-fde/handoff.json .
Read-only apart from that file.
.TP
.B live
Run from the live ISO. Lists candidate disks and asks which one to
encrypt, verifies it is FAT + btrfs, mounts the btrfs and reads the
handoff file left by
.BR prepare ,
checks the live environment has every required command, then converts:
shrink the btrfs tail, reencrypt, grow back, generate the keyfile and
install it inside the encrypted root, print the keyfile path (the live
one and the one inside the target system) and wait for Enter while any
external backup of it remains your own responsibility -- the tool never
scans for or copies to external media -- then enroll it as slot 1,
update
.IR /etc/default/grub ,
check
.IR /etc/dracut.conf.d/ ,
regenerate the initramfs and GRUB via chroot, prune the ESP to the single
EFI binary, and run a verification gate.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/beryllium-fde/handoff.json
Handoff state between phases; also tracks conversion progress.
.TP
.I /etc/cryptsetup-keys.d/cryptroot.key
The generated keyfile (0600).
.TP
.I /etc/dracut.conf.d/00-crypto.conf
Ensures the crypt/btrfs dracut modules and the keyfile are in the
initramfs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cryptsetup (8),
.BR grub-install (1),
.BR dracut (8)
